  "slug": "variants-variant-430c",
  "summary": "SeqManager flags duplicate and intermediate sequencing files to reduce genomics storage costs, reporting fast runtime.",
  "synthesis": "SeqManager is the only item here that addresses storage directly: a web-based tool that identifies duplicate and intermediate sequencing files to reduce genomics storage costs, reporting fast runtime. Its contribution is file-level redundancy detection as a management step. The remaining items are preprocessing tools for omics data rather than storage tools. metaboprep v2 extends its R package from metabolomics to Olink and SomaScan proteomics, adding a modular S7 architecture, flexible input, and automation. MetScribeR, an open-source R package with a Shiny interface, semiautomates peak finding and QC to build in-house LC-MS retention time and m/z reference libraries. The dominant thread is therefore infrastructure that reduces manual or redundant handling of omics data, though only SeqManager targets storage specifically.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-18"
}
